TakeposguardMaintenanceReleased=Attempt reconciled and expired lock released.
TakeposguardMaintenanceRecoveryDenied=Recovery denied: guard disabled, ownership changed, lock not expired or processing active. Verify before retrying.
TakeposguardMaintenanceAmbiguous=Ambiguous effects or unavailable evidence: lock preserved. Check invoice, payments, bank, stock and provider. No forced release is available.
TakeposguardMaintenancePurgeDenied=Purge denied: invalid configuration, active transaction or database error.
TakeposguardMaintenancePurged=Details purged for %s attempt(s). Tokens and outcomes are preserved.
TakeposguardPurgeHelp=Purge only SUCCESS/FAILED details completed more than %s days ago. Recent, PROCESSING/BLOCKED attempts and locked invoices are excluded. Tokens, outcomes, balances and initial validation evidence are preserved to prevent replays. Maximum 500 attempts per invocation; repeat if needed.
TakeposguardPurgeDetails=Purge old details
TakeposguardMaxAttempts=Maximum attempts per invoice
TakeposguardMaxAttemptsHelp=10 to 9999; default 1000. Limits persistent invoice tokens, including after detail purging. Increasing the limit requires administrative review.
TakeposguardAttemptLimitReached=Attempt limit reached for this invoice. No payment executed. Contact an administrator.
TakeposguardStatusPROCESSING=Processing
TakeposguardStatusSUCCESS=Successful
TakeposguardStatusFAILED=Confirmed failure
TakeposguardStatusBLOCKED=Reconciliation required
TakeposguardScheduledPurge=Purge old TakePOS Payment Guard details
TakeposguardScheduledPurgeHelp=Optional daily cleanup, disabled by default, limited to 500 confirmed attempts. Preserves tokens and validation evidence; does not release locks.
